DevOps Interview Preparation – Tool 8

AWS Fundamentals + AWS DevOps Services (0–2 Years Experience)

AWS is the most demanded cloud platform for DevOps roles.
Interviewers want to know whether you understand both core services and DevOps workflows on AWS.

 Focus: AWS Interview Questions (Mixed – Basics + DevOps)

• What is cloud computing?
• Why is AWS widely used?
• Explain AWS global infrastructure (Region, AZ, Edge location)
• What is EC2? Common EC2 instance types
• What is an AMI?
• What is a key pair and security group?
• Difference between security group and NACL
• What is S3 and why is it used?
• S3 storage classes
• What is versioning in S3?
• What is IAM?
• Difference between IAM user, group, and role
• What is an IAM policy?
• What is VPC?
• Difference between public and private subnet
• What is an Internet Gateway?
• What is a route table?
• What is AWS CLI?
• How do you configure AWS CLI?
• What is CloudWatch?
• Metrics vs logs vs alarms
• What is CloudTrail?
• ALB vs NLB
• What is Auto Scaling Group?
• What is AWS CodePipeline?
• Difference between CodeBuild and CodeDeploy
• What is blue-green deployment?
• Rolling vs blue-green deployment
• How do you monitor an application in AWS?
• Common AWS mistakes freshers make
• Real-world AWS DevOps use case

💡 Interview Tip:
If you can confidently explain:
👉 “Code → CI → Build → Deploy → Monitor on AWS”
you already sound like a real DevOps
engineer, even with 0–2 years of experience
